/-!
# Making the generic fibre geometrically reduced

A finite type morphism to an irreducible scheme becomes flat and of finite presentation with
geometrically reduced generic fibre after restricting to a nonempty open subset of the base,
making a finite universally homeomorphic base change from an integral affine scheme, and
reducing the total space.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_finiteUniversalHomeomorphism_geometricallyReduced_genericFiber`:
  the open restriction together with the finite universally homeomorphic diagram.

## Implementation notes

The total space `X'` is the reduced induced closed subscheme of `Y' ×_Y X`, and the canonical
map `g'` to `X_V = V ×_Y X` is induced by the pullback square. The canonical associativity
isomorphism identifies `Y' ×_Y X` with `Y' ×_V (V ×_Y X)`, so this also describes the second
reduced fibre product appearing in the source of `g'`. Being of finite type is expressed by
`LocallyOfFiniteType` together with `QuasiCompact`, and the conclusion on the generic fibre is
stated at every generic point of the integral scheme `Y'`.

The purely inseparable field extension produced by tag 04KT is realized on the base by a
finite subalgebra of it generated by elements a `p`-power of which already lies in the base
ring; tag 0BRA makes the corresponding map of spectra a universal homeomorphism.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0550](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0550)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits TopologicalSpace

